From 51f77c377b33a9bc807243ec027123fcb8d890a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oaradla <339301037+Oaradla@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:36:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SD bootloader: boot state file with trial start and rollback

ngCfg.json "general.stateFile" names a small state file on the card
(32 bytes, magic NGS1, CRC-32). A slot marked pending is started once
as a trial; an unconfirmed start, a failed load or a watchdog reset
falls back to the active slot and records the result, so a firmware
update cannot leave the box without a working image. The file is
rewritten in place through a direct sector write, FatFs stays
read-only. Before the jump the bootloader leaves a handover record at
0x20003FE0 for SD images that are not the original firmware.

The SD card stays powered when an SD image is started: a short supply
off phase left the card busy in ACMD41.
